"""Finite-field DH calibrated recovery ladder, reference release 5.

Tiers 1..50 use frozen rho/NFS reference targets, with Tier 50 approximately 128
classical reference bits. These are model estimates, not confidentiality proofs,
measured attack costs, elapsed-time predictions, or quantum resistance claims.

Each registered prime p has a recursive Pocklington proof with a prime factor q
of p-1 exceeding sqrt(p). The order-q generator is the first h^((p-1)/q) !=1
for h=2,3,... . Setup constants were generated once with public SHAKE256 seeds
crucible/dh-v5/setup/v1/tier-N and are embedded with their exact certificates.
See scripts/generate_dh_v5_parameters.py for reproduction. This structured
public parameter distribution is explicit; uniformity over all primes is not
claimed. Fixed groups permit reusable preparation, which solvers must report.

Honest x,r are independent uniform integers1..q-1 from OS randomness. Elements
use ceil(bit_length(p)/8) bytes. KDF binds the new domain, profile, p,q,g, pk,c,
and shared element with uint32-length framing. This source is self-contained.
Arithmetic is variable-time. The custom KDF construction is not a standardized
KEM and has no IND-CPA/IND-CCA security claim. No decapsulation oracle is exposed.
"""
from __future__ import annotations
from dataclasses import dataclass
from functools import lru_cache
import hashlib
import hmac
import math
from pathlib import Path
import secrets
from typing import Any

